tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-forge-temple/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-forge-temple/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-forge-temple/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-forge-temple/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-forge-temple/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T12:02:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T12:02:24Z","body":"@aiday-mar Please reopen this issue, as the problem has **not** been resolved, and it appears that the actual issue may not have been fully reviewed before it was closed.  \nPlease also mark it as **URGENT**, since it has been more than 5 months since the original report (5 months in which NOTHING HAS BEEN DONE ON YOUR SIDE). Some of us are paying for Copilot, and it is not acceptable to pay for a service that keeps breaking critical VS Code functionality.\n\nTo reiterate: when Copilot Chat is open, it breaks VS Code Intellisense — it gets stuck on `Loading...` and shows no results. It also prevents ESLint from updating files on save, and in many cases it prevents saving files entirely. After 3–5 seconds of attempting to save, VS Code displays:\n\n```\nGetting code actions from 'ESLint', 'GitHub Copilot Chat' ([configure](command:workbench.action.openSettings?%255B%2522editor.codeActionsOnSave%2522%255D)).\n```\n\nor if I have a rust file i ma trying to save i get \n\n```\nGetting code actions from 'ESLint', 'rust-analyzer', 'GitHub Copilot Chat' (configure).\n```\nand only if i press ```Skip``` button then it will save the file...\n\nI also get this error:\n\n```\nThe JS/TS language service crashed 5 times in the last 5 Minutes. This may be caused by a plugin contributed by one of these extensions: denoland.vscode-deno, GitHub.copilot-chat, unifiedjs.vscode-mdx Please try disabling these extensions before filing an issue against VS Code.\n\nSource: Typescript and Javascript Language Features\n```\n\nWhat is going on there? Did you lay off the developers and now rely on Copilot itself to implement new features for Copilot? It genuinely feels like the code quality of the Copilot interface has become very sloppy.\n\nThis is a severe regression affecting core editor functionality.  \nPlease escalate this internally, the current state of the Copilot Chat extension is causing major disruptions to daily development workflows.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3646205336/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/3646480496","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10885#issuecomment-3646480496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10885","id":3646480496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc7ZWOBw","user":{"login":"KristofVDB1","id":28532087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTMyMDg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28532087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1","html_url":"https://github.com/KristofVDB1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KristofVDB1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u